  "primary_source_and_locality": {
    "source": "UN Treaty Series Treaty 52717, Annex 1 and Annex 2; retained treaty text SHA256 cdd3ecccb0daf7f2f5c57cd515dc99b9d98f9cc8a5441cb9829d46d2926c9883",
    "treaty_route": "Annex 1 describes point75 in the middle of Maly Uzen and the route following Maly Uzen downstream, then the middle of Barfolomeevski reservoir, and again Maly Uzen to point76 for120.2km. Point75 is stated 0.8km SSW of control38.6; point76 is stated 3.3km NNE of control22.8. Annex2 depicts the boundary as a solid red line; treaty Articles3-4 give both annexes treaty status and state that natural river/reservoir changes do not themselves alter the boundary absent agreement.",
    "direct_map_evidence": "On the retained M-39-61 sheet (scale1:100,000; coordinate system1942; terrain1996; edition2004), the blue label 'Мал. Узень' follows the channel by the sixth contact and southward continuation. The first five fitted positions are at a mapped channel bend and its southern turn, and the mapped channel visibly continues through the labeled 'Варфоломеевское вдхр.' reservoir before the Maly Uzen continuation. This substantiates the source-specific hydrographic context described in the treaty.",
    "marker_context": "A neighboring sheet contains a nearby 22.8 annotation and a conditional grid measurement toward a candidate treaty endpoint, but the retained raster does not authenticate the annotation as the exact treaty geodetic control or prove the point76 relation. Earlier apparent 38.6 was corrected: the nearby legible label is36.6, not38.6. No endpoint-marker match is required as a universal predicate, but these readings do not resolve the six exact centers."
  },
  "per_contact_assessment": {
    "first_five": "The three adjacent centers (88758,166062..166064) and the two centers (88762..88763,166066) fall in/at the mapped river bend/channel and southern turn. The conditional fit and native image support proximity to the treaty-described hydrographic corridor, while red/dark treaty line, river bank/center, roads and overprint cannot be uniquely separated at the exact centers.",
    "sixth": "The center (88826,166117) lies by the Maly Uzen channel/embankment corridor. The label and channel continuity support locality identity, but the exact treaty stroke is not isolated at the center.",
    "original_source_conflict": "The RUS ADM2 owner and KAZ ADM1 competitor contact remain a real contrary source signal. A map label/current hydronym or local line proximity does not identify which national source's recorded polygon is correct for each cell. No country side is inferred from compass direction or from raster symbology alone."
  },
  "measurement_and_limits": {
    "grid_fit": "The corrected local affine uses visually verified projected-grid intersections and two independent held-out crossings, with residuals about1.5 raster pixels. The candidate zone-9 Pulkovo/Krasovsky conversion is explicitly conditional; it is not an asserted full datum realization or map-accuracy measure.",
    "visual_resolution": "Native embedded source images were examined (M-39-61 at3146x3678 and adjacent sheets). The actual contact crops still show tightly overlapping blue hydrography and red/dark linework. More pixels improve label legibility but do not isolate a distinct treaty centerline.",
    "unresolved_predicate": "The substantive unresolved predicate is source applicability at the exact recorded cell centers: the primary treaty and map establish a relevant boundary route, but the available map does not reliably associate each exact cell with a unique side/centerline or resolve the contrary retained KAZ ADM1 contact. This is a concrete image/source conflict, not merely a request for a modern administrative crosswalk or universal legal certificate.",
    "remaining_material_step": "No additional measurement on the retained scans is reasonably likely to disambiguate the overlapping linework at these points. A specifically located, higher-detail treaty boundary coordinate/large-scale source for this segment could change the result if available; no such artifact is part of the retained evidence. This does not assert that all external searching is exhausted."
  },
  "independent_recommendation": "The original source, official treaty text, its integral map, nearby hydronym/reservoir labels, local grid registration, datum sensitivity and native-resolution crops amount to substantial source-specific research for these six keys. I recommend these exact six for a narrowly scoped researched-unresolved proposal, subject to ordinary root review, while preserving all native holds, original source/competitor rows and package accounting. This is not positive qualification, a legal sovereignty finding, acceptance of other keys, or permission to drop adverse physical/foreign evidence."
}

